---
title: Historical memory learning loop design - superseded
---
flowchart TD
  accTitle: Historical design - Proposed memory advice and reviewed improvement retain the existing action authority
  accDescr: Historical diagram retained for earlier reports and proposals. The current production replacement is the basic computer and player contract; these semantic components are not current runtime instructions. One panel shows proposed memory advice: visible game observations enter scoped evidence, queries select applicable claims and relevant context, and unknowns lead to abstention or visible sensing. The player proposes a bounded plan; the existing supervisor and controller alone validate and execute it. A separate panel shows offline improvement: evidence-based candidate lessons undergo held-out evaluation and review before an authorized later version change. There is no automatic promotion or memory-to-game authority edge. Boxes are logical responsibilities, not extra services or an implemented persistent-memory feature.
  subgraph Advice["Proposed memory advice; existing action authority"]
    Game["Windowed CDDA"] -->|Visible observations| Evidence["Evidence: origin, scope and time"]
    Evidence --> Query["Query applicable claims<br/>and relevant context"]
    Query -->|Adequate context| Player["Player proposes a bounded plan"]
    Query -->|Unknown| Unknown["Abstain or request<br/>visible evidence"]
    Unknown -->|If available| Evidence
    Player -->|Candidate data only| Control["Existing supervisor and controller<br/>Fresh guards; sole input authority"]
    Control -->|Authorized action| Game
  end
  subgraph Improve["Offline improvement; separate acceptance"]
    Lesson["Candidate lesson from experience<br/>Context and counterexamples"] -.-> Evaluate["Held-out evaluation<br/>Transfer, retention and cost"]
    Evaluate -.->|Insufficient evidence| Revise["Reject or revise<br/>Preserve the evidence"]
    Revise -.-> Lesson
    Evaluate -.->|Qualified benefit| Review["Review a versioned change"]
    Review -.-> Version["Authorized later implementation<br/>Native acceptance when needed"]
  end
